  "model_behavior_diagnosis": {
    "finding": "Suite-head invariance is plausible under the implemented training setup; no report-overwrite or policy-aggregation bug was found in the audited artifacts.",
    "evidence": [
      "The four strategies use different selected test IDs and different predicted subtest dictionaries on all 5 runs per host.",
      "Each policy report has a distinct SHA-256 and each index entry points to its own policy-specific report.",
      "Training labels are full-run target vectors repeated for each augmented partial-observation row; the last target is the suite index.",
      "The reconstructor uses sklearn MultiOutputRegressor, which fits an independent estimator for each target; the suite head can therefore learn a nearly constant prediction even when per-component heads or inputs vary.",
      "Evaluation builds partial feature vectors from each policy selection and its probe predictions, then reads suite_index from the final output dimension.",
      "Exact per-run equality across strategies is unusual and should remain a limitation; feature-importance or controlled synthetic perturbation of the suite head would be needed to establish why it is invariant."
    ],
